{"id": "EUVD-2026-55547", "enisaUuid": "7d585d6e-fb44-351b-a3e2-0979fba30901", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsctp: close UDP tunnel sockets during netns teardown\n\nproc_sctp_do_udp_port() starts per-net SCTP UDP tunneling sockets when\nnet.sctp.udp_port is set, and stops/restarts them when the sysctl value\nchanges. The netns exit path does not stop these sockets, so a namespace\ncan be torn down while its SCTP UDP tunnel sockets are still installed.\n\nClose the UDP tunnel sockets from sctp_ctrlsock_exit() after unregistering\nthe per-net sysctl table. This prevents new sysctl writes from racing in\nwhile the sockets are being released, and closes the sockets before the\ncontrol socket is destroyed.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T11:59:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:58:55", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c29affd44e6769e3073235d4b471d9b501fa8166", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c6eb2d615210b80339548ab07c0230edaab9a6c7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8ff78591d309c50a4fdab683b68dd8d512a270dd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3bf0e349cbb4f975f35eb22753acc346b89c66a0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/37ff9794be48d0caa37687e04d09675f9c849121", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ffb2bd7ade36ec4da32c46a6eddbf4515316d08c"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9g3f-gj9q-hqjj", "CVE-2026-68161"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.66, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03cd2153-406b-3c31-8f47-b53ddd6d6bc4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.42"}, {"id": "24e446f3-c6e1-3d85-b435-d2fc6162341f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "2975897c-303d-352c-a006-2926b1e53ef9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "046c052b475e7119b6a30e3483e2888fc606a2f8 <c6eb2d6152